# ============================================================================
# SUBSTACK REDIRECT MAP  —  DO NOT DELETE. EVER.
# ============================================================================
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS
# educationprogress.org was the Substack for two years. Every old newsletter
# email, every restack, every link anyone else ever published points at
# educationprogress.org/p/[slug]. At cutover this domain starts serving the
# hub instead — so without this file, all of that goes to a 404 the day we
# launch, silently, and we find out from traffic that stops arriving.
#
# These rules forward the Substack-shaped URLs to news.educationprogress.org,
# where the newsletter now lives. This is permanent infrastructure, not
# launch scaffolding. It never gets "cleaned up."
#
# HOW IT WORKS
# Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the root of the built site. Astro
# copies everything in public/ into dist/ verbatim, so this lands at
# dist/_redirects automatically. No build step, no config.
#
# FORMAT:  /source/path   https://destination   301
#   *       in a source matches the rest of the path
#   :splat  in a destination pastes back whatever * matched
#   301     means "moved permanently" — tells Google to transfer the ranking
#
# ORDER MATTERS. First matching rule wins. Specific rules go above wildcards.
#
# ANY PATH NOT LISTED HERE IS SERVED BY THE HUB. That is deliberate: /, /about,
# /library, /research, /tools, /donate are ours now, and the hub's versions
# supersede Substack's. Do not add rules for those.
#
# TESTING: scripts/check-redirects.mjs verifies every rule below against a
# real deployment. Run it before cutover, and again right after.
# ============================================================================


# ---- Posts: THE critical rule ---------------------------------------------
# Two years of emails and restacks point here. If one rule in this file has
# to work, it is this one.
/p/*              https://news.educationprogress.org/p/:splat              301


# ---- Archive, feed, sections, tags ----------------------------------------
# /feed matters more than it looks: RSS readers and aggregators are subscribed
# to it and will silently go quiet if it dies.
/archive          https://news.educationprogress.org/archive               301
/archive/*        https://news.educationprogress.org/archive/:splat        301
/feed             https://news.educationprogress.org/feed                  301
/s/*              https://news.educationprogress.org/s/:splat              301
/t/*              https://news.educationprogress.org/t/:splat              301


# ---- Comments and Substack's internal share/image paths -------------------
# /i/ is what Substack uses for share images and embeds; these appear inside
# old emails and on social cards.
/comments/*       https://news.educationprogress.org/comments/:splat       301
/i/*              https://news.educationprogress.org/i/:splat              301


# ---- Substack's API -------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing of ours uses this. Forwarding it prevents stray 404s from embeds
# and old share widgets.
# NOTE: pull the URL inventory (see check-redirects.mjs --inventory) BEFORE
# cutover — this endpoint is how we enumerate old posts, and it stops
# answering on this domain once the swap happens.
/api/*            https://news.educationprogress.org/api/:splat            301


# ---- Subscribe ------------------------------------------------------------
# ALREADY DECIDED — see docs/domain-cutover-runbook.md in the site repo. The
# hub has no /subscribe page yet (Buttondown lands in Phase 5), so this goes
# to Substack for now. Revisit once Buttondown ships.
# Do not delete the line. /subscribe must never 404 — it is in the footer of
# every newsletter ever sent.
/subscribe        https://news.educationprogress.org/subscribe             301
